### Google Maps scraper via API externals (URLs em gmaps_urls.json; tenta a próxima se a primeira falhar)
# Suba o servidor: npm run start:dev (porta em PORT, ex.: 3003)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3003

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/health

### Listar URLs
GET {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/url

### Adicionar / trocar URL (vai para o topo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/url
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "http://100.100.105.72:8082"
}

### Zerar URLs
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/url

### Criar job
POST {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "job",
  "keywords": ["coffee shops in Austin TX"],
  "lang": "en",
  "zoom": 15,
  "lat": "30.2672",
  "lon": "-97.7431",
  "fast_mode": false,
  "radius": 10000,
  "depth": 5,
  "email": true,
  "max_time": 300
}

### Listar jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/jobs

### Status do job
@jobId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/jobs/{{jobId}}

### Download (CSV parseado em JSON)
GET {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/jobs/{{jobId}}/download

### Apagar job
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/externals/gmaps/jobs/{{jobId}}
